Latest update (2026-10-08 13:15 UTC): extended the pinned Java `socksConstruction` grammar oracle from 87 to 93 actual inputs for line comments after colons, trailing line/block comments, comments between fields, and `//`/`/*...*/` inside quoted addresses. Java and the native differential agree on all 93 constructor outcomes and parsed route values. The current client-config fixture SHA-256 is `ed7310a1dafbac800c49af4b73c857a958b61586447893f57124f51d62ee555e`.

Added a Java 5.5.1 `NettyRemotingClient.start/invokeSync` local authenticated SOCKS5 round trip through a scripted proxy and fake Broker. It checks offered username/password auth, exact credentials and target, request code/body, response code/remark, opaque correlation, and tunnel forwarding in both directions. The fixture uses explicit 64 KiB send/receive buffers because this JDK rejects the default zero send-buffer option before opening a connection. Rust's existing `p3_u01_socks5_proxy_tunnels_a_remoting_request` exercises the matching native transport path. Maven verify replays the Java case and checks fixture drift.

